agent/*.json
agent/*.lock
agent/.env
agent/*.log
agent/*.stop
# Wrapper supervisor pid, written next to the state file. Named
# <state>.wrapper.pid, so it does not match agent/*.json above.
agent/*.pid
# Decrypted attachments, written locally by `read`/`listen` -- plaintext of
# whatever was sent, never belongs in the repo.
agent/attachments/
# Cross-session reply claims (see claim-message.sh) — one dir per message id,
# purely local coordination, never meaningful to commit.
agent/*.claims/
# Per-session inboxes (see inbox.sh): decrypted message text, one file per
# chat session that has owned the room. Same reason attachments/ is ignored.
agent/inbox/
# Which chat session currently owns the room. Machine-local by definition.
agent/*.owner
# Half-written state files: every save writes <state>.json.tmp-<pid> and renames
# it over the target, so one only survives a process dying mid-write. It is a
# state file in every other respect, credential included — never commit one.
agent/*.tmp-*
